# Secrets — never commit real credentials.
#
# Deny every .env variant, then re-allow the two templates and the one real file
# that is meant to be public. The old rules named .env.appwrite and .env.*.local
# individually, which left .env.secret, .env.production and every other name a
# future contributor might pick committable — into a public repository.
#
# `.env` itself IS tracked, deliberately: it holds only the Supabase project id,
# its URL and the anon (publishable) key, all three of which ship inside the
# renderer bundle anyway and are public by design. Put anything with real
# authority — a service_role key, an Appwrite API key, a database password — in
# .env.local instead. That one is ignored (by *.local above and .env.* here),
# and Vite loads it on top of .env.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.appwrite.example

